From 82786da6a323d9668658fe31a2834e84a059d596 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 06:38:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Certificates page follow-ups: status, filters, detail modal,
 SAN badge

Implements the backend/wiring for the UI you stubbed on the
Certificates page:

- Status column now shows real day counts (days_remaining, computed
  per cert) instead of the "0 days" placeholders, with a status key
  ("expired"/"expiring_soon"/"valid") added to each row for sorting
  and filtering.
- Status + Provider filters restored, matching the Site Blocks
  dropdown pattern. Provider filtering uses a new stable provider_key
  (not the display text, which varies -- e.g. "Let's Encrypt
  (staging)") so filter values don't depend on exact wording.
- The "..." button now opens a detail modal (subject/issuer full DN,
  serial number, SHA-256 fingerprint, key type/size, full validity
  window, additional SAN names, file path) via the standard Bootstrap
  "one modal, many triggers" pattern -- each button carries the cert's
  data as data-cert-* attributes, and static/js/certificate-detail-modal.js
  populates the shared modal from whichever button triggered it.
- The +N SAN badge is now real: certs.py returns each cert's SAN names
  minus whichever one is already shown as its CN, and the badge only
  renders when there's at least one extra.
- Added a Settings > Certificates tab for the expiring-soon threshold
  (days), defaulting to 37 -- a week past Caddy's own ~30-day default
  renewal window, so "expiring soon" tends to mean renewal needs
  attention rather than just "due soon."

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
